// EXPECT: E0294 — a computed file-scope `#insert` generating anything but a library declaration
// (ADR-0184 §4)
//
//
// **Filed in `imports/invalid/` rather than `type-errors/`**, and the reason is a stage rather than an
// import: E0294 comes out of the **expanded lowering**, so `type-errors/`' harness — which runs sema on the
// *unexpanded* tree — reported `[]` for this file and failed it for not declaring what it declares. That is
// exactly why E0262, E0263, E0273 and E0290 live here too. The rule was met by moving the file, not by
// weakening the harness; this is the seventh such move.
//
// The constant half of the pair; `084-computed-insert-declarations.jr` argues the shared reasoning.
//
// A generated **constant** has no value by the time const-eval has run, because a computed operand is
// itself evaluated *by* const-eval — so the generated item arrives one phase too late to be given a value.
// That leaked out as "a file-level item has no value until jr-vm", reported against the *consumer* rather
// than the cause.
//
// The workaround is not a workaround but the mechanism that already exists: a per-OS **value** is
// `X :: #run pick();` (ADR-0181), which needs no insert at all. What an insert adds is per-OS
// *declarations*, and a library is the one the language can support today.
generated :: () -> string {
    return "VALUE :: 3;";
}

#insert #run generated();

main :: () {
}
